Compliance with the upstream license notice
-------------------------------------------

Upstream adds the following terms to Apache-2.0 section 6:

  "You are FORBIDDEN to use Shizuku as app name or use
   moe.shizuku.privileged.api as application id or declare
   moe.shizuku.manager.permission.* permission."

This project complies with all of them:

- App name: "Shizako" everywhere; never "Shizuku".
- Application id: com.churan.shizako only. No build, task, asset or
  runtime path in this repository produces or installs a package whose
  application id is moe.shizuku.privileged.api. An earlier revision did
  bundle such a placeholder ("compatibility stub") in the GitHub build to
  satisfy clients with the legacy package name hard-coded; it has been
  removed entirely, along with its module, build tasks, UI entry and
  strings. The F-Droid build never contained it.
- Permissions: com.churan.shizako.permission.* only. The library under
  "api/provider" *requests* the upstream permission name (as any
  Shizuku-API client does) so that apps can also talk to the official
  Shizuku; it declares none of moe.shizuku.manager.permission.*.
- Provider authority: com.churan.shizako.shizuku only. The upstream
  authority moe.shizuku.privileged.api.shizuku is no longer declared, so
  this app can be installed alongside the official Shizuku.
- Launcher icons: replaced, original upstream icon assets are not used.

Wire protocol constants inherited from Shizuku-API are kept as-is
(e.g. the "moe.shizuku.privileged.api.intent.extra.BINDER" Bundle key,
moe.shizuku.server.* AIDL names). Those are interoperability strings
required to talk to unmodified Shizuku-API clients, not identity claims:
they name neither this application nor any of its components.

Name and artwork
----------------

Following the same form as the upstream addendum, and to make official
builds distinguishable from repackaged copies:

- You are FORBIDDEN to use "Shizako" (including "Shizako+",
  "Shizako Plus", "Shizako Pro" or any confusingly similar variant) as
  the name of a third-party application, or as part of its package name,
  application id or permission names.
- You are FORBIDDEN to use this project's mascot artwork or launcher
  icons (manager/src/main/res/mipmap*/ic_launcher*.png and all related
  assets) for anything other than displaying Shizako itself.
- You are FORBIDDEN to distribute any non-official build under the
  application id com.churan.shizako.

Forking the code is welcome; change the name, the icons and the package
name, and everything is fine.

